On the FM-1's chip, while ALNK0's CON1 sets data 3 as a 16-bit I2S
output (nibble 0x1), a half of the buffer is LEN frames of one word
each, the word's two 16-bit halves the frame's two samples (HARDWARE-SPEC
HW-160, HW-168). Upstream plays LEN words a half as LEN / 2 frames of
two words, a 24-bit sample in each word's low bits. The patch adds
`audio_chip16` to the peripheral block, off by default: when it is on
and CON1's data 3 nibble is 0x1, a half lasts LEN frames and each word
gives two samples, the upper 16 bits first. Otherwise nothing changes.
The crate test plays_the_chips_own_layout_when_asked fails without it.

